-- title:
--   Degree over K(j) of the Γ_H(M) q-expansion field equals [SL₂(ℤ):±Γ_H(M)]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $M$ be a positive natural number and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, namely the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M)\to(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$ sending $\gamma$ to its lower right entry mod $M$. Let $F_0=$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ attached to pairs of modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(M)$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$) having integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$, with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g\neq 0$, and let $F=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange K F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) be the subfield of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to K$. Let $y\in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), i.e. $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K[[q]]$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\eta^{-24}$. Then the $K(y)$-vector space dimension of $F$, where $K(y)$ is the intermediate field of $F$ generated over $K$ by $y$, equals the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_H(M)$ together with $-1$, that is $[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_H(M)]$.
--
--   This is the fullness statement for the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(M)$: the field of modular functions for $\Gamma_H(M)$ with rational $q$-expansions, base changed to $K$, has degree over the $j$-line exactly the index of $\pm\Gamma_H(M)$, the upper bound coming from the general index estimate and the lower bound from the tower $K(j)\subseteq K\cdot F(\Gamma_0(M))\subseteq K\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ together with $[\Gamma_0(M)$-index$]=\psi(M)$. It is used in the genus computations for the full-level modular curves and in the variant of this statement for fields given with a rational structure.
